Bye.

492
00:24:50.350 --> 00:24:52.150
Aw, that was so sweet.

493
00:24:52.550 --> 00:24:53.810
I love that.

494
00:24:54.350 --> 00:24:58.370
I love knowing that they didn't do anything to his actual hair.

495
00:24:58.590 --> 00:25:00.450
She would just clip that in and out every day.

496
00:25:01.030 --> 00:25:01.510
Yeah.

497
00:25:01.690 --> 00:25:08.670
I remember Kim always having these heads with like different like forms of hair and wigs

498
00:25:08.670 --> 00:25:10.930
and braids and like whatever she was tinkering on.

499
00:25:10.930 --> 00:25:16.210
And she had like a row of like fake hair with like different versions of things, especially

500
00:25:16.210 --> 00:25:17.030
for Meredith.

501
00:25:17.350 --> 00:25:18.090
Oh, my gosh.

502
00:25:18.730 --> 00:25:21.330
Meredith was always having something done to her hair.

503
00:25:21.770 --> 00:25:22.770
So, yeah.

504
00:25:22.970 --> 00:25:25.990
Thank you so much, Kim, for the behind the scenes on that one.

505
00:25:26.130 --> 00:25:31.450
So listen, and I know we're still talking about this opening scene, but I had to bring

506
00:25:31.450 --> 00:25:32.270
up something else.

507
00:25:32.690 --> 00:25:32.870
What?

508
00:25:33.690 --> 00:25:38.490
So when Michael walks through the door, he's carrying like nine gazillion bags, right?

509
00:25:38.810 --> 00:25:43.490
And we're going to come to learn that one of them contains this steel drum that he has

510
00:25:43.490 --> 00:25:44.790
obsessed with playing.

511
00:25:44.850 --> 00:25:46.310
He's holding a box.

512
00:25:46.570 --> 00:25:48.370
He's holding bags and a box.

513
00:25:48.490 --> 00:25:51.310
And the steel drum, I think, is in the box because it's a big rectangle.

514
00:25:51.950 --> 00:25:52.390
Same.

515
00:25:53.090 --> 00:25:56.470
But it made me wonder what is in all the other bags.

516
00:25:56.470 --> 00:26:00.390
And that is an amazing deleted scene.

517
00:26:00.710 --> 00:26:01.370
Yes, Jenna.

518
00:26:01.550 --> 00:26:02.750
So those bags were gifts.

519
00:26:02.950 --> 00:26:05.210
They were like souvenirs that he bought everyone.

520
00:26:05.210 --> 00:26:08.770
They definitely look like the souvenirs you bought at the airport.

521
00:26:08.770 --> 00:26:10.770
And it's all in the deleted scenes.

522
00:26:10.770 --> 00:26:12.710
He goes around the office handing them out.

523
00:26:13.450 --> 00:26:19.190
Well, I remember doing that scene because the thing he gives Pam is a coconut bra.

524
00:26:19.510 --> 00:26:22.910
And he's like some coconuts for your coconuts.

525
00:26:23.270 --> 00:26:24.290
And I'm like, thanks.

526
00:26:24.650 --> 00:26:26.270
Then he says, do you want to see if it fits?

527
00:26:26.470 --> 00:26:32.910
And you're like, no, I'm not going to go try on this coconut bikini top right now.

528
00:26:33.150 --> 00:26:33.490
Thanks.

529
00:26:35.030 --> 00:26:35.830
Yes, exactly.

530
00:26:36.090 --> 00:26:39.350
But I remember shooting that with Steve because I couldn't get through it.

531
00:26:39.530 --> 00:26:45.090
Every time I opened it up, it was so ludicrous to me that that was the gift he gave Pam.

532
00:26:45.350 --> 00:26:46.610
It would make me laugh.

533
00:26:46.910 --> 00:26:50.890
He gives Angela Martin a lay and he puts it around her neck.

534
00:26:50.970 --> 00:26:51.970
And she's like, thank you.

535
00:26:52.070 --> 00:26:53.590
And he goes, you just got laid.

536
00:26:53.750 --> 00:26:54.910
And I'm like, no, I didn't.

537
00:26:55.450 --> 00:26:57.290
And you like rip it off, right?

538
00:26:57.370 --> 00:26:58.330
Yeah, I get really mad.

539
00:27:00.560 --> 00:27:07.360
Well, next, we're going to find out that Karen and Jim are experiencing some tension.

540
00:27:07.900 --> 00:27:08.540
Oh, yeah.

541
00:27:08.540 --> 00:27:09.760
And here is why.

542
00:27:10.580 --> 00:27:21.080
It is because Jim does not want Karen to move into an apartment that is two blocks away from his apartment, even though she's been having a really hard time finding an apartment.

543
00:27:21.080 --> 00:27:23.460
And she is currently living in a motel.

544
00:27:24.460 --> 00:27:26.160
She's at a day's end.

545
00:27:26.380 --> 00:27:28.260
That's what we learned that in a deleted scene.

546
00:27:28.440 --> 00:27:29.500
I mean, come on.

547
00:27:30.100 --> 00:27:33.440
Well, she says it down in the warehouse to Pam as well later.

548
00:27:33.740 --> 00:27:35.340
She needs to find a place to live.

549
00:27:35.940 --> 00:27:37.280
You know what I noticed?

550
00:27:37.540 --> 00:27:41.900
When Karen does her talking head, she's standing at the copier in the annex.

551
00:27:42.620 --> 00:27:46.660
Remember in the other episode, we were like, is this copier always here?

552
00:27:47.040 --> 00:27:48.600
That's where she's standing.

553
00:27:49.200 --> 00:27:53.020
That's back by Kelly's desk and Toby's desk in the annex.

554
00:27:53.020 --> 00:27:57.500
Jenna, what does it mean if your talking head is in the annex?

555
00:27:57.820 --> 00:27:58.760
What does that mean?

556
00:27:59.220 --> 00:28:00.380
What does it mean?

557
00:28:00.580 --> 00:28:04.700
I think it means you're trying to avoid somebody and you're using the copier in the annex.

558
00:28:05.140 --> 00:28:05.560
Yeah.

559
00:28:06.000 --> 00:28:10.580
Jenna, speaking of deleted scenes, there's another great runner between Phyllis and Stanley.

560
00:28:10.840 --> 00:28:14.600
Because, you know, Stanley says he doesn't get all of his bonus and he's not going to work.

561
00:28:14.720 --> 00:28:17.160
Not a lick until he gets that bonus money.

562
00:28:17.160 --> 00:28:23.460
And it starts driving Phyllis crazy because he won't answer his phone.

563
00:28:23.720 --> 00:28:25.900
She has a phenomenal talking head.

564
00:28:26.040 --> 00:28:27.840
So that's in the DVD deleted scenes.

565
00:28:28.820 --> 00:28:31.520
I remember shooting those and they were very funny.

566
00:28:31.520 --> 00:28:35.120
And I love any time there's a dynamic between Phyllis and Stanley.

567
00:28:35.580 --> 00:28:41.140
So now we're in Michael's office and he's playing the steel drum for Pam.

568
00:28:41.600 --> 00:28:44.300
He's telling her all about his trip to Jamaica.

569
00:28:44.300 --> 00:28:52.740
Jamaica, he's explaining that everyone in Jamaica just relaxes all day and they party all the time.

570
00:28:53.080 --> 00:28:53.720
They love it.

571
00:28:53.960 --> 00:28:54.260
Yeah.

572
00:28:54.400 --> 00:28:55.900
He's like, write this down, Pam.

573
00:28:56.460 --> 00:28:58.560
Pina colada is every day at 3 p.m.

574
00:28:58.800 --> 00:29:02.340
Like he is just he is definitely not ready to go back to work.

575
00:29:02.780 --> 00:29:06.860
And this is when Pam breaks the news to him that they have to do inventory,

576
00:29:07.120 --> 00:29:12.400
which is something that he was hoping to avoid by going on vacation.

577
00:29:12.400 --> 00:29:15.420
And she says, Michael, we can't do inventory without you.

578
00:29:15.580 --> 00:29:16.240
We had to wait.

579
00:29:16.420 --> 00:29:18.120
It has to be done today.

580
00:29:20.030 --> 00:29:21.750
He is so bummed out.

581
00:29:21.910 --> 00:29:23.470
He hates doing inventory.

582
00:29:23.470 --> 00:29:24.450
He says it's boring.

583
00:29:24.450 --> 00:29:26.450
So he decides to make it a party.

584
00:29:26.730 --> 00:29:30.930
And he tells Angela, get the party planning committee together.

585
00:29:30.930 --> 00:29:34.150
We're going to have a luau this afternoon.

586
00:29:34.150 --> 00:29:36.370
And she is not having it.

587
00:29:36.370 --> 00:29:37.110
She's like, what?

588
00:29:37.550 --> 00:29:45.130
At four minutes, you get a shot of a real snarky expression from Angela Martin about this luau that she now has to throw.

589
00:29:45.350 --> 00:29:47.390
But please look at the outfit.

590
00:29:47.950 --> 00:30:00.510
Crazy blouse with a high collar, froofy collar, argyle sweater in shades of beige and brown, brown skirt, ponytail with what Kim Ferry and I called the sloop.

591
00:30:01.570 --> 00:30:05.090
This is a classic Angela Martin outfit, if I have to say so myself.

592
00:30:05.730 --> 00:30:13.810
Well, lady, we had a fan question from Katie Wegman, who is asking, is the shirt that you're wearing the same one you wore in Benihana Christmas?

593
00:30:13.870 --> 00:30:15.630
Because it looks almost identical.

594
00:30:16.050 --> 00:30:17.190
No, it is not.

595
00:30:17.310 --> 00:30:25.790
This season, the wardrobe department had bought me all of these high collared froofy blouses, which only live this season and never come back.

596
00:30:27.030 --> 00:30:28.470
But that is not the same one.

597
00:30:28.630 --> 00:30:30.290
It's yet another froofy blouse.

598
00:30:30.510 --> 00:30:40.470
Well, now we go into the conference room, Angela, because Michael wants everyone to watch a video slideshow on Island Life and a big thing happens.

599
00:30:41.330 --> 00:30:43.810
Karen does not sit next to Jim.

600
00:30:44.390 --> 00:30:44.670
Yeah.

601
00:30:45.470 --> 00:30:46.510
It's serious.

602
00:30:46.790 --> 00:30:47.890
This fight is serious.

603
00:30:48.250 --> 00:30:54.570
And then while they're watching this slideshow, Pam spots Jan on the beach with Michael.

604
00:30:54.950 --> 00:30:57.190
But he denies that it's her.

605
00:30:58.130 --> 00:30:58.950
Jenna, hold up.

606
00:30:58.950 --> 00:31:00.510
I have written down here.

607
00:31:00.690 --> 00:31:02.230
Pam pulls a Michael.

608
00:31:02.510 --> 00:31:04.750
Pam, why did you call it out?

609
00:31:05.230 --> 00:31:05.750
Why?

610
00:31:06.150 --> 00:31:08.250
I mean, that's something Michael would do.

611
00:31:08.430 --> 00:31:14.310
I feel like a normal move for Pam would be to notice Jan, totally know it was her and not say anything.

612
00:31:14.630 --> 00:31:17.430
And instead be like, oh, right.

613
00:31:17.630 --> 00:31:19.950
And then maybe go be chatty with Jim about it later.

614
00:31:19.950 --> 00:31:24.770
But instead, Pam points at the screen and goes, wait, is that Jan?

615
00:31:25.090 --> 00:31:26.190
That's Jan.

616
00:31:26.490 --> 00:31:29.910
And I feel like that's something Michael or Dwight would have done normally.

617
00:31:30.970 --> 00:31:32.730
I totally hear that.

618
00:31:32.950 --> 00:31:35.790
I think that's a valid analysis.

619
00:31:36.130 --> 00:31:41.630
I will say I think it was probably so shocking to Pam that she just blurted it out.

620
00:31:41.870 --> 00:31:45.030
I mean, it's to see Jan in the picture.

621
00:31:45.310 --> 00:31:48.610
She just I imagine she was just like, oh, my God.

622
00:31:49.610 --> 00:31:51.110
OK, OK, fair enough.

623
00:31:51.330 --> 00:31:51.950
OK, I get it.

624
00:31:52.090 --> 00:31:55.330
Well, we had a fan question about this scene, Angela, from Maren Allen.

625
00:31:55.670 --> 00:32:03.330
She wrote in to say, my 13 year old daughter Dakota pointed out that when Pam notices Jan and Michael's vacation slideshow,

626
00:32:03.510 --> 00:32:07.950
Michael says that she's actually a German woman named Ergel Gru.

627
00:32:07.950 --> 00:32:17.010
And my daughter would like to know if this name was improvised and if it has anything to do with Steve's Despicable Me character, Gru.

628
00:32:17.270 --> 00:32:18.730
I had the same question.

629
00:32:19.050 --> 00:32:20.390
So I looked it up.

630
00:32:20.670 --> 00:32:25.210
This episode was filmed in 2007, back from vacation.

631
00:32:25.950 --> 00:32:28.310
Despicable Me came out in 2010.

632
00:32:28.570 --> 00:32:34.850
So then I researched animation production and how long it takes a movie like Despicable Me to be made.

633
00:32:35.030 --> 00:32:37.090
And they take three to five years.

634
00:32:37.090 --> 00:32:45.930
So it is possible that there was an overlap that Steve was doing voiceover while we were filming on The Office.

635
00:32:45.930 --> 00:32:46.910
It's possible.

636
00:32:47.350 --> 00:32:48.370
Oh, my gosh.

637
00:32:48.530 --> 00:32:50.370
And maybe that is why.

638
00:32:51.090 --> 00:32:55.930
Because in the script, it says Earl Gru, but he says Ergel Gru.

639
00:32:56.470 --> 00:32:58.890
Maybe it was like on his mind.

640
00:32:58.890 --> 00:33:01.010
And that's why he said Gru.

641
00:33:01.370 --> 00:33:03.010
Let's move it on, Michael.

642
00:33:03.010 --> 00:33:07.890
Michael, I mean, he's got to tell someone, right?

643
00:33:08.210 --> 00:33:13.130
He's so excited to tell Packer that Jan went with him to Jamaica.

644
00:33:13.410 --> 00:33:14.850
And Packer doesn't believe him.

645
00:33:14.970 --> 00:33:15.690
He's like, no way.

646
00:33:15.970 --> 00:33:17.390
So Michael's like, you know what?

647
00:33:17.410 --> 00:33:18.290
I'll send you a picture.

648
00:33:19.910 --> 00:33:23.990
And Packer's email is Packer at Dunder Mifflin.

649
00:33:24.710 --> 00:33:28.750
But he sends it to Packaging at Dunder Mifflin.

650
00:33:28.930 --> 00:33:35.030
And how this all goes down in the scene is so great because Michael is like, did you get it?

651
00:33:35.190 --> 00:33:35.910
Hit refresh.

652
00:33:36.290 --> 00:33:36.830
Hit refresh.

653
00:33:37.330 --> 00:33:39.770
And Packer is like, no, I didn't get it.

654
00:33:39.870 --> 00:33:43.630
And then all of a sudden he says, oh, I just got it from someone else.

655
00:33:45.230 --> 00:33:47.610
And then Michael's like, wait, wait, what?

656
00:33:47.730 --> 00:33:48.310
Who else?

657
00:33:48.490 --> 00:33:48.730
What?

658
00:33:48.970 --> 00:33:52.830
And then Michael realizes he has sent it to the wrong place.

659
00:33:53.010 --> 00:34:01.090
He sent it to Daryl in the warehouse, who has clearly forwarded it to Packer or someone else who forwarded it to Packer.

660
00:34:01.090 --> 00:34:02.970
But it is out, basically.

661
00:34:03.770 --> 00:34:10.030
I want to point out that that line at the end when Packer says, how do I get you out of this picture?

662
00:34:10.530 --> 00:34:11.570
That was an improv.

663
00:34:11.910 --> 00:34:13.570
That was a Dave Koechner ad.

664
00:34:13.790 --> 00:34:16.010
Yeah, that's Dave Koechner at his beSt.

665
00:34:16.330 --> 00:34:19.970
After Michael gets off the phone with Packer, he is freaked out.

666
00:34:20.150 --> 00:34:21.830
Oh, he's freaking the heck out.

667
00:34:22.010 --> 00:34:23.990
He needs to do damage control.

668
00:34:24.350 --> 00:34:25.850
So he runs.

669
00:34:26.070 --> 00:34:28.590
He sprints to the warehouse.

670
00:34:28.590 --> 00:34:31.230
We had a fan question from Anna Rhodes.

671
00:34:31.570 --> 00:34:37.610
She says, at 7 minutes, 20 seconds, where is that hallway that Michael is running down to get to the warehouse?

672
00:34:38.250 --> 00:34:40.070
Anna, I had the same question.

673
00:34:40.090 --> 00:34:42.890
So I did some digging, but Jenna, I know you did too.

674
00:34:43.050 --> 00:34:44.310
And you went to Kentopedia.

675
00:34:44.550 --> 00:34:45.290
So what do you got?

676
00:34:46.070 --> 00:34:46.510
All right.

677
00:34:46.690 --> 00:34:51.010
Kent told me that that is the hallway where our writers work.

678
00:34:51.470 --> 00:34:53.830
He is running down the writer's hallway.

679
00:34:53.970 --> 00:34:56.750
All those doors you see are writer's offices.

680
00:34:56.750 --> 00:35:03.030
And when he turns the corner and he runs through that doorway, he is running into Mindy Kaling's office.

681
00:35:03.350 --> 00:35:04.310
Is he really?

682
00:35:04.690 --> 00:35:05.070
Yes.

683
00:35:05.410 --> 00:35:05.790
Oh, my God.

684
00:35:05.850 --> 00:35:07.350
I thought that was Kent's office.

685
00:35:07.510 --> 00:35:08.410
Oh, my gosh.

686
00:35:08.530 --> 00:35:08.670
Okay.

687
00:35:08.730 --> 00:35:09.310
I love that.

688
00:35:09.730 --> 00:35:11.410
Well, I have a little catch, Jenna.

689
00:35:12.430 --> 00:35:15.850
He runs past a woman sitting at a desk, right?

690
00:35:16.090 --> 00:35:17.730
Right at the very beginning of his sprint.

691
00:35:17.990 --> 00:35:19.790
Well, that is Mary Wall.

692
00:35:19.790 --> 00:35:22.190
And she was our executive producer assistant.

693
00:35:22.470 --> 00:35:23.870
She's in an orange hoodie.

694
00:35:24.370 --> 00:35:25.790
She was the beSt.

695
00:35:25.950 --> 00:35:27.250
She did everything for us.

696
00:35:27.350 --> 00:35:29.910
I love that we put Mary in that scene.

697
00:35:30.090 --> 00:35:33.110
So I guess they just made all the writers close their doors.

698
00:35:33.570 --> 00:35:35.370
But they let Mary keep working.

699
00:35:35.370 --> 00:35:36.790
And they just shot that scene.

700
00:35:36.950 --> 00:35:37.950
Steve ran right past her.

701
00:35:38.230 --> 00:35:38.370
Yeah.

702
00:35:38.370 --> 00:35:43.530
And the desk that Mary is sitting at is directly outside of the writer's room conference room.

703
00:35:43.810 --> 00:35:45.150
They had their own conference room.

704
00:35:45.270 --> 00:35:50.510
And Steve starts his sprint right in the doorway of that writer's room conference room.

705
00:35:50.590 --> 00:35:53.170
And he runs right past Mary at the desk outside of it.

706
00:35:53.310 --> 00:35:57.210
Well, after he runs into Mindy's office, obviously, it's a dead end.

707
00:35:57.210 --> 00:35:58.870
So they had to cut there.

708
00:35:58.870 --> 00:36:05.310
Then Steve had to go down into the warehouse, walk up the steps, and get into that little

709
00:36:05.310 --> 00:36:08.830
fake box at the top of the stairs that actually leads nowhere.

710
00:36:09.530 --> 00:36:11.230
And then come back down.

711
00:36:11.650 --> 00:36:12.210
Yes.

712
00:36:12.490 --> 00:36:17.050
And then they would yell action, and he would come running back down the stairs as if he

713
00:36:17.050 --> 00:36:19.090
had actually come from somewhere.

714
00:36:20.670 --> 00:36:23.210
So then he runs into Daryl's office.

715
00:36:23.210 --> 00:36:28.530
And I believe, Angela, this is the first time we've seen Daryl's office in the warehouse,

716
00:36:28.530 --> 00:36:30.450
where we've actually gone inside of it.

717
00:36:30.590 --> 00:36:36.690
In this scene, at 7 minutes 38 seconds, Daryl is eating a giant plate of food.

718
00:36:36.770 --> 00:36:40.570
We had a fan question from Dave H.

719
00:36:40.770 --> 00:36:42.290
and Andrea Petit Bell.

720
00:36:43.010 --> 00:36:45.630
What is up with Daryl's massive plate of food?

721
00:36:46.010 --> 00:36:48.830
When Michael goes in to ask him about the picture.

722
00:36:49.330 --> 00:36:53.330
Well, Angela, it is not in the script that Daryl is eating.

723
00:36:53.650 --> 00:36:55.790
And usually it is.

724
00:36:55.930 --> 00:36:57.830
Usually it is scripted that we're eating food.

725
00:36:58.710 --> 00:37:00.270
Here's why I went to look.

726
00:37:00.490 --> 00:37:05.410
When I looked at that plate of food, it 100% looked like the stuff they would serve us at

727
00:37:05.410 --> 00:37:06.110
craft services.

728
00:37:06.350 --> 00:37:07.830
I thought the same thing.

729
00:37:08.110 --> 00:37:09.270
Jenna, oh my God.

730
00:37:09.270 --> 00:37:15.090
When I looked at it, I was like, is Craig, as Daryl, just holding his lunch?

731
00:37:15.350 --> 00:37:17.110
Or like a snack he made?

732
00:37:17.810 --> 00:37:18.290
Yeah.

733
00:37:18.290 --> 00:37:24.870
Yeah, I think he was hungry and he was having a plate of food and they were like, oh, you

734
00:37:24.870 --> 00:37:26.110
should just eat that in the scene.

735
00:37:26.310 --> 00:37:28.090
That food brought me back.

736
00:37:28.270 --> 00:37:30.410
I had a sense memory when I saw the plate.

